WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.589
From sci-fi originals to hard-hitting dramas
to superlative horror films, the year 2017

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:08.830
delivered a bumper crop of excellent flicks
for film lovers.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:12.700
The year was so chock full of cinematic wins
that some critics have had trouble trimming

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.419
down their lists of favorites.

00:00:14.419 --> 00:00:19.340
Even so, there's no doubt that these movies
are part of what made 2017 such a memorable

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.460
year for movies.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:24.699
Split
Pretty much no one saw it coming, but M. Night

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:28.420
Shyamalan's surprise hit Split is among the
best films of the year.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:33.280
The taut thriller follows a group of young
women abducted by a man with multiple personalities.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.800
Their struggle for dominance threaten to either
upend his plans… or make things even worse

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.040
for his captives.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.220
"Everybody just take a minute!"

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.920
Critics have hailed it as an unexpected return
to form for Shyamalan, and a big part of the

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.140
film's buzz comes from its twist ending.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:54.129
It isn't just the shocking final act that
makes Split so much fun—actor James McAvoy

00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:58.309
ties it all together with a tour de force
performance.

00:00:58.309 --> 00:01:01.620
Get Out
Helmed by debuting feature director Jordan

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:06.110
Peele, this comedy-horror hybrid follows the
increasingly frightening misadventures of

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:10.380
a young man venturing into the suburbs to
meet his girlfriend's parents.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.660
The fact that they're an interracial couple
underscores both the funniest and creepiest

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:20.080
moments of the film, and soon our hero finds
himself under the town's sinister spell just

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.990
as the dangers of his hosts become clear.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:24.240
"Get out!"

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:26.780
"Sorry, man."

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.060
"Get out!"

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.560
There's a reason everyone's been talking about
Get Out since its release; see it yourself

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.650
and find out why.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:38.980
Logan
Although Hugh Jackman has been celebrated

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.830
for his portrayal of Wolverine for the better
part of two decades, none of those outings

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:46.960
have truly captured the angst and rage that
help make the character so poignant in the

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:47.960
comics.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:53.110
That all changes with Logan, a loose adaptation
of the Old Man Logan comics arc that finds

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:58.690
our hero in a grim wasteland largely devoid
of mutants, called upon to defend a mysterious

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:01.980
girl targeted by a passel of bloodthirsty
villains.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:07.140
A brooding Western road trip with claws, Logan's
been hailed by critics as a fitting farewell

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.720
for Jackman—and perhaps the best entry in
the X-Men franchise to date.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:16.530
Beauty and the Beast
Disney's winning streak continued in 2017

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.930
with the box office bonanza that was their
Beauty and the Beast live-action remake.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:25.460
The faithful remake of its animated predecessor
was a must-see for movie fans because it introduced

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:30.590
a new all-star cast, updated visual dynamics,
and a few new songs and in-jokes to enjoy.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:35.140
It was a rare movie that could be truly enjoyed
by audiences of all ages, and arrived as one

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:38.500
of the year's most successful movies as a
result.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.360
Wonder Woman
After 75-plus years of taking down baddies

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.900
in the comics pages, and one supporting appearance
in Dawn of Justice, Wonder Woman finally got

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:52.530
her shot at solo blockbuster glory in 2017—and
she may have single-handedly saved the DC

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:53.740
Extended Universe.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:57.850
Wonder Woman did everything it needed to and
then some, serving as an effective origin

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:02.430
story as well as a superhero adventure that
stood on its own while continuing to lay the

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.470
groundwork for Justice League.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:08.480
Considering how underwhelming Justice League
turned out to be, it looks like Wonder Woman

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:14.040
is going to be carrying the DCEU on her very
capable shoulders from here on out.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.320
Baby Driver
With its eclectic soundtrack and insanely

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:21.480
impressive stunts, Edgar Wright's Baby Driver
is an exciting action flick.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:25.660
The pic centers on a young crook named Baby,
who works as a getaway driver for a smarmy

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.270
crime boss named Doc.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:31.710
Suffering from tinnitus, Baby drowns out the
constant droning with an incredible collection

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:36.410
of iPods, and while he's grooving to the tunes,
he's able to weave in and out of traffic,

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:40.840
dodge cars and avoid police pursuit by doing
180s in alleyways.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:45.319
But Baby's life gets a little more complicated
when he falls head over heels for a beautiful

00:03:45.319 --> 00:03:47.870
waitress, which makes him want to straighten
his life out.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:52.100
But he's got one more job on deck, working
with a who's who of psycho killers.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:56.410
Needless to say, the robbery doesn't go as
planned, and Baby is forced to take a stand

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.090
to save everything he loves.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:02.100
With its dance-like action and its cool character
line-up, the film has got a little something

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:06.819
special for everyone and arrived as an immediate
standout for the year.

00:04:06.819 --> 00:04:10.020
Dunkirk
Of Christopher Nolan's greatest achievements,

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.990
Dunkirk is right up there with Inception and
The Dark Knight.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:17.709
The nail-biting World War II thriller tells
the story of a real-life military retreat.

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:22.340
Roughly 400,000 Allied troops were trapped
on a French beach, completely surrounded by

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:26.530
the Nazis, and the only thing keeping our
heroes from home was the English Channel.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:31.290
Unfortunately, the beach was too shallow to
accommodate military-sized vessels, so English

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:35.960
civilians sprang into action, sailing to Dunkirk
in their yachts and fishing boats.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.410
It was an incredible moment in history, and
Nolan does a masterful job of capturing the

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:41.410
suspense.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:45.250
In true Nolan fashion, the story is divided
into three interwoven narratives which are

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.090
all ultimately connected.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:51.500
Audiences are put in the middle of the battlefield
and feel the same desperation of those soldiers,

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.970
waiting for a boat to arrive with a chance
of rescue.

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:58.850
It
Andy Muschietti's It isn't the first adaptation

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:00.600
of Stephen King's weighty novel.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:05.550
In 1990, Tim Curry made horror history by
playing Pennywise the Dancing Clown, the Derry

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:07.800
demon with a fondness for floating.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:12.350
"Kiss me, fat boy!"
(laughs)

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:17.500
But with Bill Skarsgård wearing the carnival
makeup, things are a lot darker and bloodier

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.590
in the new take.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:23.350
The first of a two-part tale, It tells the
story of "The Losers' Club," a group of outcast

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:26.870
kids who are beaten by bullies and plagued
by horrible home lives.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:30.699
But when they're together, these kids are
pretty powerful—and they need as much strength

00:05:30.699 --> 00:05:34.360
as possible when they find themselves facing
a flesh-eating clown.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:38.230
The Losers eventually head into the sewers
to end the evil that's been plaguing their

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.560
town for years.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:43.880
And under all the gore and grime, behind the
monstrous apparitions and evil sinks, there's

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:48.430
a lot of heart in this movie…even if the
creepy clown wants to eat everyone.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:52.120
Blade Runner 2049
While it's become one of the most influential

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:57.120
sci-fi movies ever made, when Blade Runner
hit theaters in 1982, it divided critics and

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.610
flopped at the box office.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:03.300
35 years later, Denis Villeneuve's sequel
has been similarly unsuccessful at the box

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:07.949
office, but it completely impressed critics
with its stunning visuals and intensely philosophical

00:06:07.949 --> 00:06:08.949
plot.

00:06:08.949 --> 00:06:13.590
The film's dynamic landscape feels equal parts
terrifying and fabulous, and even beyond the

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:17.729
gorgeous imagery is a movie still grappling
with and building on the same meaty themes

00:06:17.729 --> 00:06:20.840
from the first film—namely, the nature of
humanity.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:25.270
With Ryan Gosling as K, a blade runner hunting
for answers about his past and the truth about

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:29.960
the android race known as "replicants," the
story explores the depths of the human soul.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:34.050
So, while the film may have not been a commercial
success this time either, we can count on

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:39.870
Blade Runner 2049 to inspire the sci-fi scene
for generations to come as well.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:44.070
I, Tonya
Directed by Craig Gillespie, I, Tonya is an

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:49.490
examination of what really happened in 1994
when ice skater Nancy Kerrigan was attacked

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:54.050
before the US Figure Skating Championship
in Detroit, and how one woman was at the center

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:55.930
of it all: Tonya Harding.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:07:00.790
Played to perfection by Margot Robbie, Harding
comes off as a tragic anti-hero, caught between

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:05.169
an abusive mother, a violent husband, and
her desperate need to succeed in a snobby

00:07:05.169 --> 00:07:06.970
sport that treats her like dirt.

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:08.940
"Maybe you should pick another sport."

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:13.080
"Suck my d---."

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:16.960
Surrounded by creeps and idiots, she claws
her way to the top, only to see everything

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:18.680
come tumbling down fast.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:23.100
You might already have an opinion on the notorious
ice queen, but thanks to Robbie's powerhouse

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:27.259
performance we actually come to sympathize
with this woman—who's so often reduced to

00:07:27.259 --> 00:07:29.639
a simple, trashy villain.

00:07:29.639 --> 00:07:33.900
Star Wars: The Last Jedi
While it's controversial among some Star Wars

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:39.500
fans, The Last Jedi cleaned house at the box
office and used its Force powers to win over

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.280
most every critic in the galaxy.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:45.680
Picking up pretty much immediately after The
Force Awakens, the film finds Rey desperately

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:49.810
trying to convince a world-weary Luke Skywalker
that the Resistance needs his help.

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:54.479
But the old Jedi is holding on to some secrets,
and refuses to leave his deserted planet,

00:07:54.479 --> 00:07:58.750
frustrating Rey and causing her to seek answers
from her old enemy, Kylo Ren.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:03.259
In addition to the main plot, The Last Jedi
takes us to some incredible new worlds and

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:08.009
pays homage to the originals while setting
up an exciting new future for the franchise.

00:08:08.009 --> 00:08:12.360
Thor: Ragnarok
For the most part, the Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:17.080
has delivered solid, entertaining films…with
the exception being the Thor franchise.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:20.960
While the character always had potential,
the first two films didn't quite do justice

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:22.410
to the God of Thunder.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:27.870
So thank Odin for Taika Waititi whose Ragnarok
is an apocalyptic good time.

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:32.099
The plot follows Thor as he's trying to stop
Hela from taking over Asgard.

00:08:32.099 --> 00:08:36.919
Unfortunately, his superhero plans don't pan
out, and after the hammer is crushed into

00:08:36.919 --> 00:08:41.419
tiny pieces, he finds himself imprisoned on
a planet where he's forced to do battle with

00:08:41.419 --> 00:08:42.539
the Incredible Hulk.

00:08:42.539 --> 00:08:47.069
What results is possibly the funniest movie
in the entire Marvel franchise and one with

00:08:47.069 --> 00:08:48.839
a surprising amount of heart.

00:08:48.839 --> 00:08:50.120
"That doesn't sound right."

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.120
"Well, it's true."

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:56.029
Unlike the previous two films, Ragnarok actually
has something to say about the destructive

00:08:56.029 --> 00:09:00.670
influence of colonialism and how great nations
often hide their bloody pasts.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:04.470
And most importantly, Thor is no longer a
Shakespearean straight man.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:09.080
Instead, he's a good-natured goof who's forced
to truly reckon with his own godhood, with

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:12.629
a few werewolves and fire demons in the mix.

00:09:12.629 --> 00:09:16.160
Phantom Thread
10 years after There Will Be Blood, Paul Thomas

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:20.310
Anderson reunited with Daniel Day-Lewis for
Phantom Thread, a period drama that marks

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:23.410
the last time Day-Lewis steps in front of
a movie camera.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:27.619
The story follows his powerful and obsessive
dressmaker who goes through women like they're

00:09:27.619 --> 00:09:31.779
spools of thread until he meets his match
in a waitress who turns the artist's life

00:09:31.779 --> 00:09:32.800
upside down.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:37.949
Soon, the relationship goes from sweet to
toxic, allowing Day-Lewis to unleash all of

00:09:37.949 --> 00:09:39.529
his thespian powers along the way.

00:09:39.529 --> 00:09:43.410
While it's lacking the fire and brimstone
of There Will Be Blood, Phantom Thread is

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:48.360
just as powerful in its suave and simmering,
mild-mannered English way and marks a fitting

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:51.519
end to Day-Lewis' illustrious career.

00:09:51.519 --> 00:09:55.059
The Disaster Artist
Widely considered one of the worst movies

00:09:55.059 --> 00:10:00.300
ever made, The Room has left audiences howling
for years with its bizarro scenes and nonsensical

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.800
dialogue, courtesy of Tommy Wiseau.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:03.940
"You are lying.

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:05.019
I never hit you.

00:10:05.019 --> 00:10:07.899
You are tearing me apart, Lisa!"

00:10:07.899 --> 00:10:13.360
An oddball auteur who wrote, directed, and
starred in this epically awful film, Wiseau

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:17.490
has long been one of cinema's craziest and
most mysterious characters.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:21.660
He's been treated as a laughingstock and a
villain, but according to The Disaster Artist,

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:24.970
maybe he's just the ultimate embodiment of
the Hollywood dream.

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:29.449
Directed by and starring James Franco, the
film depicts the relationship between aspiring

00:10:29.449 --> 00:10:34.699
actor Greg Sestero and Wiseau, an out-of-control
egomaniac with incredible amounts of cash

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:40.199
and zero ability to memorize lines.

00:10:44.329 --> 00:10:49.259
Wiseau hopes to become an A-list star, but
when he's rejected time and again, he decides

00:10:49.259 --> 00:10:53.339
to make his own movie, sucking Greg into the
world's weirdest film shoot.

00:10:53.339 --> 00:10:57.160
While it would be really easy to make Wiseau
look completely foolish, Franco gives a much

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:01.529
more layered performance that's being called
one of his all-time best.

00:11:01.529 --> 00:11:05.540
The Shape of Water
Guillermo del Toro is a master at telling

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:10.269
enchanting tales, as seen in films like Pan's
Labyrinth, The Devil's Backbone, and Crimson

00:11:10.269 --> 00:11:11.269
Peak.

00:11:11.269 --> 00:11:15.790
And now the director has crafted what might
be his magnum opus with The Shape of Water,

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:19.790
a film that looks like Creature from the Black
Lagoon but feels more like Beauty and the

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:20.790
Beast.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:25.120
This film follows a mute janitor who works
at a government lab and discovers an Amphibian

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.410
Man locked away in the bowels of the building.

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:31.589
Despite their very apparent differences, the
two form a bond, and soon there's a romance

00:11:31.589 --> 00:11:36.029
brewing, one threatened by Cold War intrigue
and a vicious military officer.

00:11:36.029 --> 00:11:40.709
The result is a truly magical movie with gorgeous
direction and moving performances from its

00:11:40.709 --> 00:11:42.260
leading duo.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:45.829
All the Money in the World
Ridley Scott managed to turn what could've

00:11:45.829 --> 00:11:51.470
been a show-stopping scandal into a point
of positive buzz through sheer force of will.

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:55.619
After Kevin Spacey was accused of multiple
accounts of inappropriate behavior against

00:11:55.619 --> 00:11:59.829
minors, it seemed there wasn't enough money
in the world to save the director's true-life

00:11:59.829 --> 00:12:00.829
thriller.

00:12:00.829 --> 00:12:05.230
But Scott quickly recalibrated by recasting
Spacey's role with Christopher Plummer and

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:10.269
re-shot 22 scenes with just six weeks to go
until the film was due in theaters.

00:12:10.269 --> 00:12:14.720
Not only did he complete the ultra-ambitious
adjustment in time, but critics were also

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:19.059
highly impressed with Plummer's misanthropic
performance as the billionaire who refused

00:12:19.059 --> 00:12:21.339
to pay ransom for his kidnapped grandson.

00:12:21.339 --> 00:12:26.170
As a result, the movie which could've become
a casualty of the 2017 reckoning was actually

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:28.399
one of the year's most impressive productions.

00:12:28.399 --> 00:12:32.360
The Post
Based on a true story, Steven Spielberg's

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:37.819
The Post follows Washington Post owner Katharine
Graham and editor Ben Bradlee as they debate

00:12:37.819 --> 00:12:42.139
whether to publish the Pentagon Papers, leaked
documents that exposed the U.S. government's

00:12:42.139 --> 00:12:43.870
lies about the Vietnam War.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:47.500
With pressure coming down hard from the White
House, the two must grapple with concepts

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:51.920
like the value of a free press, knowing full
well their decision could wreck the paper

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:52.920
or worse.

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.170
"We could all go to prison."

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:58.649
An old-school movie from an old-school master,
The Post brilliantly jumps back and forth

00:12:58.649 --> 00:13:01.879
from historical epic to a comedy to crackling
thriller.

00:13:01.879 --> 00:13:06.100
The A-list stars are on the top of their game,
and more importantly, in an era when "fake

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:11.019
news" and divisive politics rule the day,
The Post is a timely reminder of the importance

00:13:11.019 --> 00:13:12.300
of journalism.

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:13.300
Thanks for watching!

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.519
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:13:15.519 --> 00:13:17.370
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

